# First executable milestone

The first slice demonstrates source → AST → type checking → value, with useful
errors at each stage. Keeping two types makes type checking observable without
inventing a large language.

```hql
40 + 2
```

Run `cargo run --locked -- eval '40 + 2'` to get `42`, or
`cargo run --locked -- check examples/answer.hql` to get `Int`.
`true + 1` is rejected before evaluation. Checking an overflowing addition
succeeds because checking does not execute it.

The scanner stays inside the parser until syntax justifies extracting it.
[Current behavior](../models/behavior/expressions.md) declares exact grammar,
limits, errors, and CLI behavior. [[design-direction]] covers ideas that are
explicitly outside this milestone. Return to [[hql]].
